# Hitchcock Harness settings. setup.sh copies this file to .env.local the first time.
# Every line is commented out: the defaults below apply. To change one, remove the "#" and edit the value,
# then restart the app. No keys or passwords are needed: Alma uses your own Claude login, and Higgsfield is
# signed in through Claude Code's /mcp. Two keys are optional: the remote-access key (under "The app") and the
# reserve key at the end. setup.sh makes .env.local readable by you only.

# ---- Folders (all inside this app's folder by default)

# The studio folder: the film workspace Alma works in (rules, tools, films). Default: <app>/studio
# HARNESS_FILM_REPO=/path/to/hitchcock-harness/studio

# The folder every film lives under; the films list is empty while it is missing. Default: <studio>/assets
# HARNESS_DRIVE_ROOT=/path/to/hitchcock-harness/studio/assets

# The cross-film library (faces, voices, characters, locations). Default: <studio>/assets/library
# HARNESS_LIBRARY=/path/to/hitchcock-harness/studio/assets/library

# Where delivered cuts go, as "<YYYY-MM-DD> <Title>/" folders; several folders separated by ":".
# Default: <studio>/assets/final-cuts
# HARNESS_FINAL_CUTS=/path/to/hitchcock-harness/studio/assets/final-cuts

# The film rules, one note per stage ("Flow v3.2 - 12 Release.md" …). Default: <studio>/flow
# HARNESS_FLOW_DIR=/path/to/hitchcock-harness/studio/flow

# The record of where each film was posted. Default: <studio>/published-links.md
# HARNESS_PUBLISHED_LINKS=/path/to/hitchcock-harness/studio/published-links.md

# Other film workspaces whose films should also be listed, separated by ":". Default: none
# HARNESS_OTHER_REPOS=

# ---- Programs (found on your PATH by default)

# The Claude Code program. Default: "claude" on the PATH (else ~/.local/bin/claude)
# HARNESS_CLAUDE_BIN=/path/to/claude

# ffmpeg and ffprobe for renders and thumbnails. Default: the ones on the PATH
# HARNESS_FFMPEG=/path/to/ffmpeg
# HARNESS_FFPROBE=/path/to/ffprobe

# The Python the studio's tools run with. Default: <studio>/.venv/bin/python (made by setup.sh), else python3
# HARNESS_PYTHON=/path/to/python3

# Blender, for the previz stage (studio/tools/previz reads this). Default there: /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender
# BLENDER_BIN=/Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender

# ---- Alma

# Alma runs with Claude Code's permission prompts off (nobody sits at a terminal to answer them).
# "ask" switches her to accept-edits: file edits go through, any other tool that would ask is refused.
# Default: unset (permissions off)
# HARNESS_ALMA_PERMISSIONS=ask

# Close a film's idle Alma after this many milliseconds (she resumes on the next message). Default: 1200000 (20 min)
# HARNESS_ALMA_IDLE_MS=1200000

# Extra folders Alma may read and write, separated by ":". Default: none
# HARNESS_ALMA_ADD_DIRS=

# 1 = record messages to a file instead of starting Claude Code (for testing the app). Default: unset
# HARNESS_ALMA_DRYRUN=1

# ---- The app

# The port is set where the app starts: "-p 8800" in package.json, or another one given by hand
# (npm run dev -- -p 8810). The app reads the port it really runs on and gives Alma and the Settings page that
# address, so nothing here needs to change with it. HARNESS_PORT is used only by the app's scripts that run
# outside the server (tests, tools). Default: 8800
# HARNESS_PORT=8800

# 1 = render the 480p of the cut after every change (by default it is made when you ask for it)
# HARNESS_AUTO_480P=1

# Remote access (optional, e.g. from your phone). The app listens on this Mac only (127.0.0.1), so another device
# reaches it only through a tunnel you run on this Mac (for example a cloudflared quick tunnel to the app's port).
# Unset = every request that comes through a tunnel is refused. Set a long random value (16 characters or more) and
# open <the tunnel's address>/unlock?t=<value> once on the other device: it keeps a cookie made from the key (not the
# key itself) for 90 days. Anyone with the key and the tunnel's address can use the app, Alma included.
# HARNESS_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# Tailscale (optional, off unless set): with `tailscale serve` (your tailnet only, never Funnel) in front of the app,
# the Tailscale logins named here reach it from their own devices without the key. Comma-separated, e.g.
# you@example.com. Funnel, any other tunnel, and a request that does not come from a tailnet address still need the key.
# HARNESS_TAILNET_USERS=

# ---- Optional: the reserve switch

# Settings > "Reserve: API credits" can switch Alma from your Claude plan to API credits, for when the plan's limit is
# reached. It needs an API key from your Claude Console organization, here in .env.local (never in .env.example,
# never committed). Read each time the switch is used: adding it needs no restart. Default: unset (the switch stays off)
# HARNESS_RESERVE_API_KEY=
